================================================================================
PARITY NOTES (web/src/components/ui/Tooltip.tsx -> native)
================================================================================
- Data source: web `useId` -> TooltipController.surfaceID (stable per-instance id,
  the a11y identity + once-only telemetry key); no HTTP in the view (bound via the
  P1/S8 state-holder).
- Faithful-parity: the web <Tooltip> is a pure presentational primitive (no fetch,
  no React-Query, no Promise). It therefore has no loading/error/stale/offline
  branch; reproducing such chrome would fabricate states the source lacks. The REAL
  branches are all reproduced and tested: resting (opacity-0 scale-95) / revealed
  (opacity-100 scale-100, on hover/tap/programmatic), single-line vs multiline
  (whitespace-nowrap vs max-w-[260px]), the four sides (top/bottom/left->leading/
  right->trailing), the empty-content guard (never reveal a blank box), and reduced
  motion (motion-reduce -> animation disabled). Same stance as siblings HelpTooltip
  (0216), ContextMenu (0206), DataTableColumnMenu (0210).
- Inverted-surface contract (web bg-gray-900 text-gray-100 dark:bg-gray-100
  dark:text-gray-900) reproduced token-only: paint with Color.TS.textPrimary, write
  with Color.TS.bg — both flip together across light/dark/high-contrast.
- aria-describedby -> the trigger's accessibility hint (TooltipProjector.describedBy
  join); decorative card hidden from VoiceOver to avoid a duplicate announcement.
- i18n (P1/S10): the web source routes NO t() call (content is caller-supplied,
  already-localized); the surface is anonymous. TooltipStrings facade + Tooltip.strings
  document this; no hardcoded English in the surface.
- Telemetry (P1/S11): view.opened emitted once per content-bearing instance with the
  slug "Tooltip".

